# Interactive Scene Auditor & Production Telemetry Plan

This plan addresses the "Lipsync Bottleneck" by providing a detailed timing audit and implementing a high-speed "Skip Lipsync" production path. We will also finalize the **Interactive Scene Auditor** to allow instant, localized dub previews.

## 📊 Stage Duration Audit (86-Minute Film on 1050 Ti)

I have analyzed the historical file timestamps to determine exactly where our time is spent:

| Stage | Process | Duration (86m Film) | % of Total |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **S1** | Vocal Separation (Demucs) | ~8 Minutes | 1% |
| **S2** | Transcription (Whisper) | ~63 Minutes | 5% |
| **S3** | Translation (Llama CPU) | ~16 Minutes | 1% |
| **S4** | TTS Synthesis (XTTS) | ~150 Minutes | 13% |
| **S6** | **Lipsyncing (MuseTalk)** | **~18-22 Hours** | **80%** |

> [!CAUTION]
> **The Lipsync Trap**: MuseTalk currently processes at ~2 frames per second on your hardware. For an 86-minute film (129,000 frames), this stage alone takes nearly a full day of GPU compute.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **"Skip Lipsync" Production Path**: Given your feedback on resolution vs. time, I am adding a **"Fast Dub"** mode. This will perform Stages 1-5 and immediately output a dubbed video with original visuals, saving you 20+ hours of render time.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. UI Upgrades (Dashboard Enhancements)
#### [MODIFY] [main_ui.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/app/main_ui.py)
*   **Production Tab**: Add a checkbox: `[ ] Skip Lipsync (Generate Fast Dub)`.
*   **Auditor Tab**: Implement the **Instant Auditor** with:
    - **Timeline Slider**: Select `Start Time` (0 to Film Duration).
    - **Scene Selector**: Link to Master Workspace `1776007462`.
    - **Deep Preview Toggle**: Option to include Lipsync just for the selected 30s scene.

### 2. Pipeline Optimization
#### [MODIFY] [pipeline.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/app/pipeline.py)
*   **Skip Logic**: If `skip_lipsync` is True, the pipeline will jump from `S5 (Audio Mix)` directly to `S7 (Finalize)`.
*   **Data Inheritance**: If a Preview starts with a `master_ws` selected, it will clone existing `translated_segments.json` and `tts_segments/` that fall within the time window.

